<title>BELGIUM: Belgian dredger sucks up World War One bomb.</title>
<headline>Belgian dredger sucks up World War One bomb.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>A dredger working off the Belgian port of Zeebrugge sucked up a British mortar bomb dating from World War One on Wednesday, the Belgian navy said.</p>
<p>The 100mm (four-inch) bomb lodged in the ship's suction system but did not explode. The device was later made safe by anti-mine personnel, the navy said in a statement.</p>
